## 6. Class Definitions

### 6.1 Complete Class Syntax

```dale
CLASS ClassName
    SUPERCLASS : SuperClassName
    INSTANCE VARIABLES :
        varName1 .
        varName2 TypeName .
        varName3 ;
        varName4 TypeName .
    CLASS METHODS :
        classMsg: $ param1
            ($
                RETURN result;
            $)
    INSTANCE METHODS :
        EXTERNAL
        instanceMsg: $ param1
            ($
                RETURN result;
            $)
        instanceMsg2: $ p1 put: $ p2
            ($
                varName1 <- p1;
                return varName1;
            $)
        instanceMsg3
            ($
                RETURN varName1;
            $)
    ENDCLASS.
```

### 6.2 Class Components

| Component | Required | Description |
|-----------|----------|-------------|
| `CLASS` | Yes | Keyword starting class definition |
| `ClassName` | Yes | Identifier for the class |
| `SUPERCLASS :` | No | Inherited class (default: `object`) |
| `INSTANCE VARIABLES :` | No | Instance variable declarations |
| `CLASS METHODS :` | No | Methods on the class object |
| `INSTANCE METHODS :` | Yes | Instance method definitions |
| `EXTERNAL` | No | Domain switch for instance methods |
| `INTERNAL` | No | Domain switch for instance methods |
| `ENDCLASS.` | Yes | Terminates class definition |

### 6.3 Instance Variable Declarations

```dale
INSTANCE VARIABLES :
    simpleVar .
    typedVar Integer .
    var1 ;
    var2 String .
    var3 .
```

- Each variable ends with `.`
- Type annotations are optional (ignored in current implementation)
- Multiple variables can be separated by `;`

### 6.4 Method Definitions

```dale
methodName: $ paramName
    ($
        statements;
        return result;
    $)
```

Or with multiple parameters:

```dale
methodName: $ p1 put: $ p2
    ($
        statements;
        return result;
    $)
```

Or without parameters:

```dale
methodName
    ($
        statements;
        return result;
    $)
```

### 6.5 Domain Switches

```dale
INSTANCE METHODS :
    EXTERNAL
    method1: $ param
        ($ ... $)
    
    INTERNAL
    method2: $ param
        ($ ... $)
    
    method3
        ($ ... $)
```

- `EXTERNAL`: Default domain
- `INTERNAL`: Internal methods (affects self/environment context)

